module bindings.c.prefix_offset_unchecked;

// The C library's bounded prefix-comparison contract: strncmp(3) and
// strncasecmp(3), and the library wrappers named for them, verify only the n
// bytes they are asked to compare, so after a comparison succeeds the last
// byte the code may read on the compared pointer is the one at offset n --
// for the shortest input the guard admits, the string's own terminator. A
// branch that advances the pointer further reads bytes the comparison did not
// prove present and, for that shortest input, steps past the end of the
// buffer.
//
// The fact is emitted by the C frontend (ccPrefixOffsetObservations,
// internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go) from the syntax tree: the
// comparison in an if's condition pairs only with arithmetic in that if's own
// consequence, the arithmetic must name the compared pointer itself, and the
// offset must be a literal beyond the longest prefix the condition compares
// on that pointer -- the fact fires only when no arm of the condition can
// have verified the bytes the advance reads, so a disjunction of unequal
// lengths leaves the shorter arm's own over-read unreported. A nested if
// comparing the same pointer again tightens the bound inside its own
// guarded body -- an if's consequence, and a while's or for's body, whose
// condition is checked before every iteration -- and a guard that
// subscripts the compared pointer at or past
// the compared length consults that byte itself and clears the fact.
//
// Residuals, all false-negative except the last: only the `== 0` and `!call`
// success spellings and decimal compared lengths establish a bound, the
// pointer must be spelled identically at the comparison and the arithmetic
// with the offset on its right, and only an if's consequence counts as the
// pairing scope, so a loop that is itself the outermost guard comparing a
// prefix, with a body that advances the pointer, is not labelled. The
// pairing is by spelling, so a branch that reassigns
// the compared pointer and then advances the name still reports.
binding prefixOffsetUnchecked {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.kind == "any" and node.analysis == "prefix_length.offset_past_verified"
  emit issue code.UncheckedPrefixOffsetArithmetic at node
}
